hes","Wildlife","Off-Road Adventures"],mustDo:"Relaxing on Playa Delfines and exploring the Mayan ruins of El Rey",description:"A vibrant tropical paradise on the Yucatán Peninsula, offering pristine turquoise waters, luxury resorts, and a robust kosher scene backed by Chabad of Cancun.",bestTimeToVisit:"December to April",nearestAirport:"Cancún International Airport (CUN)",airportDistance:"12 miles",attractions:[{name:"Playa Delfines",description:"Spectacular public beach with powdery white sands, expansive Caribbean ocean vistas, and the iconic colorful Cancún photo sign."},{name:"Punta Cancún (Hotel Zone & Faro)",description:"The premier northern tip of the Hotel Zone featuring the historic red-and-white Punta Cancún Lighthouse, calm wave-protected turquoise shallows at Playa Caracol, and premier shopping and entertainment."},{name:"El Rey Archaeological Zone",description:"Ancient Mayan ruin site situated right inside the Cancun Hotel Zone, featuring 47 excavated structures including a pyramid-shaped temple dating to around 250 A.D."},{name:"Isla Mujeres",description:"Small Caribbean island about 13 km off the coast of Cancun. It is reached by a roughly 20-minute ferry from Puerto Juárez or the Hotel Zone, and offers beaches and an underwater museum."}],activities:[{name:"Snorkeling the Cancun Underwater Museum",description:"Dive amongst underwater sculptures designed to promote reef life."},{name:"Ziplining through the Jungle",description:"Take high-flying adventure tours in nearby natural eco-parks."}],hotels:[{name:"Kempinski Hotel Cancun (formerly The Ritz-Carlton)",description:"Legendary beachfront luxury resort in the Hotel Zone offering timeless marble elegance, private beach cabanas, and world-class service. About 1.5 km (a 20-minute walk) from Chabad of Cancun at Plaza Kukulcan.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Retorno del Rey 36, Zona Hotelera, Km 14, 77500 Cancún, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 998 881 0808",website:"https://www.kempinski.com/en/hotel-cancun",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/kempinski-hotel-cancun-formerly-the-ritz-carlton-cancun.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 1.5 km (roughly a 20-minute walk) from Chabad of Cancun at Plaza Kukulcan, Km 13."},{name:"Grand Fiesta Americana Coral Beach Cancun",description:"Award-winning 5-star beachfront resort in Punta Cancun featuring expansive multi-tier lagoon pools and pristine calm waters at Playa Caracol.",price:"$$$$",address:"Blvd. Kukulcan Km 9.5, Punta Cancun, Zona Hotelera, 77500 Cancún, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 998 881 3200",website:"https://www.coralbeachcancunresort.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/grand-fiesta-americana-coral-beach-cancun.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.8 km (10-minute walk) from Dag Dag, a kosher dairy and fish restaurant at Km 8.5. Chabad of Cancun is about 4 km south at Km 13 (taxi on weekdays; not walkable for Shabbat)."},{name:"JW Marriott Cancun Resort & Spa",description:"Iconic luxury resort on Cancun’s turquoise beach featuring sprawling oceanfront pools and palm-shaded terraces; about 0.5 km from Ember Kosher restaurant.",price:"$$$$",address:"Blvd. Kukulcan Km 14.5, Lote 40-A, Zona Hotelera, 77500 Cancún, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 998 848 9600",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/cunjw-jw-marriott-cancun-resort-and-spa/overview/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/jw-marriott-cancun.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Marriott's own dining page lists Ember Kosher about 1.2 km away. Chabad of Cancun at Plaza Kukulcan (Km 13) is about 2 km, roughly a 28-minute walk."},{name:"SLS Playa Mujeres",description:"Sophisticated beachfront sanctuary in gated Playa Mujeres with marina berths, catamaran charters, and swim-up suites. Offers Liora, the resort’s own kosher dining program (kosher breakfast and poolside service, extra daily fee).",price:"$$$$$",address:"Paseo Mujeres, Manzana 1 Supermanzana 3 Cancún, 77400 Cancun, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 998 313 3716",website:"https://slshotels.com/playa-mujeres/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/sls-playa-mujeres-cancun.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Runs its own glatt kosher dining program, Liora (Mehadrin certification, Rabbi Simantob Rafael Nigri), booked as a per-person add-on. About 15 km from Chabad of Cancun, so not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"NIZUC Resort & Spa",description:"A tranquil 29-acre secluded sanctuary at Punta Nizuc with private mangroves, protected coral reefs, and reflecting pools. Dedicated kosher kitchens with IKM-certified kosher meals for breakfast, lunch and dinner.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Blvd. Kukulcan Km 21.26, Nizuc, Zona Hotelera, 77500 Cancún, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 998 891 5700",website:"http://www.nizuc.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/nizuc-resort-spa.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Has its own IKM-certified kosher kitchens with separate meat, dairy and parve cookware, serving kosher meals (per the hotel). About 8 km from Chabad of Cancun; not walkable for Shabbat."}],restaurants:[{name:"Dag Dag Kosher Fish & Grill",description:"Fresh local catch, grilled whole fish, ceviche, and Israeli salads prepared under strict rabbinic oversight.",kosher:!0},{name:"Ember Kosher Cancun",description:"Upscale Glatt Kosher dining in the Hotel Zone with exceptional ambiance, prime steaks, attentive service, and Mexican specialties (accommodates custom hard-shell and cigar-style tacos).",kosher:!0}],chabad:[{name:"Chabad Jewish Center of Cancun",address:"Plaza Kukulcan, Blvd. Kukulcan Km 13, Zona Hotelera, 77500 Cancún, Q.R., Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Mendel Druk",phone:"+52 998 188 6300",website:"http://www.jewishcancun.com",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Dag Dag Kosher Fish",address:"Blvd. Kukulcán Km 8.5, Punta Cancún, Zona Hotelera, Cancún",kashrus:"Chabad of Cancun (Kosher Fish / Parve)",phone:"+52 998 890 6680",website:"http://www.jewishcancun.com",type:"Fresh Fish / Mexican Seafood / Salads"},{name:"Ember Kosher Cancun",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d3-ember-kosher-cancun.webp",address:"Blvd. Kukulcán Km 15.1, Zona Hotelera, Cancún",kashrus:"Chabad of Cancun (Mehadrin Glatt Meat)",phone:"+52 998 217 5057",website:"https://theemberkosher.com",type:"Upscale Steakhouse / Mexican Grill"}],kosherGroceries:[],transportation:"City buses (R-1 and R-2) run 24/7 along Blvd. Kukulcán for ~MX$12 cash. Taxis operate on set zone rates throughout the Hotel Zone, but airport taxis are steep (~MX$650 / $38 USD from Punta Cancun to Terminal 3). Uber is approved to operate in Quintana Roo, but taxi unions still clash with app drivers, especially around the airport.",travelTips:["Hotel Zone Public Transit (Buses vs Taxis): Public city buses (routes R-1 and R-2) run up and down Blvd. Kukulcán 24 hours a day for only ~MX$12 in cash. They are safe, air-conditioned, frequent, and significantly more affordable than private hotel taxis for traveling between downtown, Punta Cancún, and southern hotel zone beaches.","Cancun Airport (CUN) Terminal 3 Logistics: The Priority Pass lounge in Terminal 3 (The Lounge) is landside, before the security checkpoint, so visit it before going through security. Note that Mexico does not conduct exit passport control checks when departing on international flights.","Airport Taxi Union Rates: Taxis from Punta Cancun or the Hotel Zone to Cancun Airport Terminal 3 charge steep union-regulated prices (~MX$650 / $38 USD for a <30-minute ride). ADO express buses from downtown Cancun offer a budget alternative for solo travelers.","Punta Cancún Stroll & Luggage Drop: If you have a late afternoon or evening departure, you can arrange luggage drop-off at Chabad of Cancun, spend a relaxing afternoon walking around Punta Cancún and enjoying an early dinner at Ember Kosher, and take a 25-minute taxi directly to CUN Airport.","Punta Cancún Access & Beach Conditions: Punta Cancún (around kilometer 9–9.5) marks the natural bend where the coastline transitions from quiet, wave-protected north-facing waters (Playa Caracol) to breezy eastern surf beaches (Playa Gaviota Azul). The scenic red-and-white Punta Cancún Lighthouse can be reached via a pleasant seaside walk starting from Playa Caracol.","Shabbat & Kosher Meal Planning: Shabbat meal packages should be reserved early in the week with Chabad of Cancun at Plaza Kukulcán (km 13). If staying in northern Punta Cancún resorts, prepare for a ~40-minute walk south along the pedestrian sidewalk or reserve accommodations located within immediate walking distance of Plaza Kukulcán."],nearby:["Isla Mujeres","Playa del Carmen","Puerto Morelos","Riviera Maya"]},{id:"cozumel",name:"Cozumel",state:"Quintana Roo",country:"Mexico",region:"Caribbean",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/d953ee98844dd728.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"4h 15m",Miami:"1h 50m",Jerusalem:"15h 45m",Paris:"10h 30m",London:"9h 45m"},weather:"☀️ 83°F",experiences:["Beaches","Wildlife","National Parks"],mustDo:"Snorkeling at Palancar Reef and visiting the Cozumel Chabad Center",description:"A world-class diving destination characterized by breathtaking coral reefs, crystalline waters, and a very popular Jewish traveler community.",bestTimeToVisit:"March to June",nearestAirport:"Cozumel International Airport (CZM)",airportDistance:"2 miles",attractions:[{name:"Palancar Reef",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/c9333b13d02a0c3f.webp",description:"World-renowned marine sanctuary along the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef, celebrated for towering coral pinnacles, deep swim-through caves, and crystal-clear underwater visibility."},{name:"Chankanaab Beach Adventure Park",description:"Adventure park inside Cozumel's National Reef Marine Park with a beach, a lagoon, reef snorkeling and scuba diving, a tropical garden, prehispanic replicas, a Mayan hut and a kids' playground. Some activities, such as dolphin swims, cost extra."},{name:"Punta Sur Ecological Park",description:"Protected ecological reserve at Cozumel's southern tip, home to the historic Celarain lighthouse, crocodile observation towers on Colombia Lagoon, and white-sand beaches."},{name:"Villa Maya Nature Reserve",description:"Lush private ecological reserve nestled in Cozumel’s interior jungle along Camino a Villa Maya, dedicated to rainforest conservation, native biodiversity, and peaceful nature walks."},{name:"Zona Arqueológica San Gervasio",description:"Ancient pre-Columbian Mayan archaeological site on Cozumel, long considered a pilgrimage center dedicated to the goddess Ixchel, with several Mayan structures to explore amid island wildlife."},{name:"Benito Juárez Park (Parque Benito Juárez)",description:"Central waterfront plaza and gathering point in downtown San Miguel de Cozumel, steps from the ferry terminal, with a historic clock tower, a shaded gazebo, a fountain, benches and the colorful COZUMEL sign, surrounded by shops, cafés and restaurants."},{name:"Parque Andrés Quintana Roo (Parque Municipal)",description:"Spacious civic park in Cozumel with a monument to independence figure Andrés Quintana Roo, open-air event pavilions, tree-lined walking areas, spaces where children play, and lively evening gatherings with live music and local island atmosphere."}],activities:[{name:"Scuba Diving at Palancar",description:"Explore deep coral tunnels and marvel at giant sponges and tropical fish."},{name:"Catamaran Sailing & Snorkeling",description:"Sail by catamaran along Cozumel's coast to snorkel at reef sites and visit shallow sandbar areas such as El Cielo, known for its calm, clear waters."}],hotels:[{name:"Casa Mexicana Cozumel",description:"Vibrant, charming waterfront boutique hotel located on the San Miguel malecón with a tranquil oceanfront plunge pool terrace. The absolute top choice for Shabbat-observant travelers on Cozumel due to its short walking distance to Chabad.",price:"$$",address:"Av. Rafael E. Melgar 457, Centro, 77600 San Miguel de Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 987 872 9090",website:"https://casamexicanacozumel.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/casa-mexicana-cozumel-cozumel.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.6 km (8-minute walk) from Chabad of Cozumel and Alma Kosher on 5a Avenida Sur; Chocolatte and Fuego kosher are within about 0.7 km. Rooms have a small refrigerator. Chabad of Cozumel lists it as a recommended hotel."},{name:"Presidente InterContinental Cozumel Resort & Spa",description:"The premier 5-star luxury resort on the island, boasting an extraordinary private marine reef, secluded ocean coves, and private dive boat pick-up directly from its pier.",price:"$$$$",address:"Carr. Chankanaab Km 6.5, Zona Hotelera Sur, 77600 Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 987 872 9500",website:"https://www.ihg.com/intercontinental/hotels/us/en/cozumel/czmha/hoteldetail",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/presidente-intercontinental-cozumel.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 6 km south of Chabad of Cozumel downtown; taxi needed, not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"The Westin Cozumel",description:"Modern, high-rise luxury hotel with magnificent ocean views on Cozumel’s tranquil northern coast, featuring private plunge pool cabanas, rooftop sky lounge, and water sports.",price:"$$$",address:"Carretera Costera Norte Km 4.8, 77613 Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 987 872 9200",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/czmwi-the-westin-cozumel/overview/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/the-westin-cozumel-cozumel.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Rooms have a mini fridge. About 5 km north of Chabad of Cozumel downtown; taxi needed, not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"Hotel B Cozumel",description:"Boutique oceanfront retreat combining chic Mexican artisanal design with seaside hammocks, an oceanfront hot tub, and direct snorkeling access into a thriving coral lagoon.",price:"$$",address:"Carretera Costera Norte Km 2.5, Zona Hotelera Norte, 77600 Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 55 9708 0015",website:"https://www.hotelbcozumel.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/hotel-b-cozumel-cozumel.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 3 km from Chabad of Cozumel (roughly a 45-minute walk along the coast road, or a short taxi). Rooms have a mini fridge (guest report)."}],restaurants:[{name:"Alma Kosher Restaurant - Cozumel",description:"Popular Glatt Kosher restaurant and grill at the Chabad Center serving fresh fish, burgers, shawarma, and Mexican tacos.",kosher:!0},{name:"Jerusalem Kosher Cozumel",description:"Charming restaurant serving authentic Mexican and Israeli dishes prepared fresh under Chabad.",kosher:!0},{name:"Chocolatte Espresso Bar - Kosher",description:"Kosher dairy espresso bar and cafe serving quality coffee, sandwiches, salads, and fresh baked goods under Chabad (popular lunch stop with NY-level pricing).",kosher:!0},{name:"Fuego Restaurant Cozumel",description:"Waterfront kosher dining overlooking the Caribbean ocean, serving steaks and fish; kashrus certified and verified by the Rabbi of Chabad of Cozumel.",kosher:!0}],chabad:[{name:"Chabad of Cozumel",address:"5a Avenida Sur, entre Calle 1 Sur y Adolfo Rosado Salas, Centro, 77668 Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Dudi Caplin",phone:"+52 987 104 0770",website:"http://chabadcozumel.com",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Alma Kosher Restaurant - Cozumel",address:"5a Avenida Sur, C. 1 Sur y, Centro, 77668 Cozumel, Q.R., Mexico",kashrus:"Chabad of Cozumel (Glatt Meat & Fish)",phone:"+52 987 104 0770",website:"http://chabadcozumel.com",type:"Israeli Grill / Mexican Tacos / Fresh Fish",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-alma-kosher-restaurant-cozumel.webp"},{name:"Jerusalem Kosher Cozumel",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d3-jerusalem-kosher-cozumel.webp",address:"Av. Rafael E. Melgar at Calle 10 Norte (2nd floor of mall), San Miguel de Cozumel",kashrus:"Chabad of Cozumel (Glatt Meat)",phone:"+52 1 987 869 5333",type:"Israeli Grill / Mexican"},{name:"Chocolatte Espresso Bar - Kosher",address:"Calle 1 Sur 58, Centro, Cozumel",kashrus:"Chabad of Cozumel (Chalav Yisrael / Kosher Dairy)",phone:"+52 987 104 0770",website:"http://chabadcozumel.com",type:"Dairy Cafe / Espresso Bar / Sandwiches & Salads"},{name:"Fuego Restaurant Cozumel",website:"https://fuegocozumel.com",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d3-fuego-cozumel.webp",address:"125 Av. Rafael E. Melgar, between Calle 2 & Calle 4, Cozumel",kashrus:"Orthodox Kosher Supervision (verified by Rabbi of Chabad Cozumel)",phone:"+52 987 871 9770",type:"Waterfront Steaks & Fish / Ocean Views"}],transportation:"Uber is approved in Quintana Roo and operates in Cozumel. Taxis operate on fixed union zone rates. From Cozumel Airport (CZM), shared shuttles to downtown/Chabad are cheaper than private airport taxis. Scooter and jeep rentals are popular for coastal drives.",travelTips:["Airport Arrival & Shared Shuttles: When arriving at Cozumel International Airport (CZM), skip the expensive private airport taxis and buy a ticket for the shared shuttle at the counter inside the terminal for the quick ride to Chabad of Cozumel or downtown hotels.","Chabad Hospitality & Luggage Drop: Chabad of Cozumel is exceptionally welcoming, staffed by energetic bochurim, and happily accommodates luggage storage for travelers needing a safe place for bags before checking in or heading on a catamaran excursion.","Climate & Passing Showers: Stepping off flights from dry Mexico City into Cozumel brings an immediate wave of tropical Caribbean humidity. Mid-afternoon rain showers occur frequently but typically clear within 10 to 15 minutes.","Interior Transportation: When heading into Cozumel’s interior to visit Villa Maya or San Gervasio ruins, arrange a taxi driver in advance to wait for you or agree on a scheduled return pickup, as cell reception can be spotty and return cabs are rarely available on the highway.","Interior Access Road Closures: The interior transversal roads and connecting unpaved paths leading to inland reserves like Villa Maya and San Gervasio can occasionally close without notice due to private land maintenance, municipal forestry works, or heavy rainfall. Confirm road conditions with your hotel concierge or local drivers prior to departure.","Ferry Logistics from Playa del Carmen: Passenger ferries between Playa del Carmen and San Miguel de Cozumel depart hourly from morning until night, operated alternately by Ultramar and Winjet. Purchase one-way tickets instead of round-trips so you can board whichever ferry leaves next on your return rather than waiting an extra hour for your original company.","Reef-Safe Sunscreen Rule: Cozumel Reefs National Park (Palancar, Colombia), Chankanaab and most cenotes and eco-parks allow only biodegradable (reef-safe) sunscreen. Bring biodegradable sunscreen or wear UV-protective rashguards."],nearby:["Playa del Carmen","Riviera Maya","Punta Sur","San Miguel Centro"]},{id:"playa-del-carmen",name:"Playa del Carmen",state:"Quintana Roo",country:"Mexico",region:"Caribbean",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/fec3ae65a750d1d6.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"4h 00m (to CUN)",Miami:"1h 45m (to CUN)",Jerusalem:"15h 35m",Paris:"10h 20m",London:"9h 35m"},weather:"☀️ 83°F",experiences:["Beaches","Waterfalls","Off-Road Adventures"],mustDo:"Strolling down Quinta Avenida and swimming in spectacular cenotes",description:"A chic, trendy coastal resort town on the Riviera Maya, combining beautiful Caribbean coastlines with lively dining, eco-adventure parks, and a welcoming Chabad house.",bestTimeToVisit:"December to April",nearestAirport:"Cancún International Airport (CUN)",airportDistance:"35 miles",attractions:[{name:"Quinta Avenida (5th Avenue)",description:"Lively pedestrian-only street in Playa del Carmen running parallel to the beach for over 4 km, lined with shops, cafes, restaurants, fashion boutiques, art galleries and artisan stalls.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d-quinta-avenida-5th-avenue.webp"},{name:"Cenote Azul",description:"Breathtaking open-air freshwater limestone pool bordered by jungle limestone ledges, crystal-clear turquoise waters, natural cliff-jumping perches, and friendly nibbling fish."},{name:"Cenote Cristalino",description:"Natural cenote near Playa del Carmen with clear water, a cave, and a popular swimming and snorkeling spot."},{name:"Cenote Chaak Tun",description:"Underground cenote cave system near Playa del Carmen featuring stalactites and stalagmites, explored on guided snorkeling tours through low-lit caverns and natural pools."},{name:"Nearby Tulum Archaeological Ruins (Day-Trip)",description:"13th-century walled Mayan city on 12-meter (about 40-foot) cliffs overlooking the turquoise Caribbean Sea, roughly a 45-minute to one-hour drive south of Playa del Carmen."},{name:"Xcaret Park",description:"World-class eco-archaeological theme park celebrating Mexico’s rich folklore, subterranean river swimming, butterfly pavilions, coral aquariums, and the celebrated México Espectacular evening performance."}],activities:[{name:"Cenote Swimming & Diving",description:"Float in the mystical, crystal-clear underground rivers of the Riviera Maya."},{name:"ATV & Zipline Adventure",description:"Ride ATVs off-road through rugged jungle trails in the Riviera Maya, with options to add ziplines and stop at a cenote along the way."}],hotels:[{name:"Devossion by Live Aqua Playa del Carmen",description:"Adults-only, all-inclusive beachfront resort (formerly the Grand Hyatt Playa del Carmen, rebranded in 2025) on the beach at Calle 26 in downtown Playa del Carmen, a short walk from 5th Avenue and Mamitas Beach. Pools, spa and several à la carte restaurants. Note: guests must be adults (no children), and the all-inclusive dining is not kosher.",price:"$$$$",address:"1a Avenida Esquina Calle 26, Col. Centro, 77710 Playa del Carmen, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+1 800 343 7821",website:"https://www.fiestamericanatravelty.com/en/devossion/hotels/devossion-playa-del-carmen",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d4-grand-hyatt-playa-del-carmen.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Adults-only all-inclusive, so not for families with children. About 1.6 km (roughly a 22-minute walk) from Chabad of Playa del Carmen on 20 Avenida; Hilula kosher bakery is about 1.2 km."},{name:"The Fives Downtown Hotel & Residences, Curio Collection by Hilton",description:"Chic, modern urban residential hotel located on 10th Avenue in the heart of downtown Playa del Carmen, featuring residential suites with full kitchenettes and a stunning rooftop infinity pool lounge overlooking the Caribbean.",price:"$$$",address:"Avenida 10 Norte entre Calle 2 y 4, Centro, 77710 Playa del Carmen, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 984 206 5500",website:"https://www.hilton.com/en/hotels/czmmsqq-the-fives-downtown-hotel-and-residences-playa-del-carmen/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d3-the-fives-downtown.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.3 km (5-minute walk) from Chabad of Playa del Carmen on 20 Avenida. Suites have a kitchen with stove, microwave and refrigerator; some units have full-size refrigerators."},{name:"The St. Regis Kanai Resort, Riviera Maya",description:"Architectural marvel elevated on stilted circular pavilions over a 620-acre mangrove reserve with private plunge pools, beach cabanas, and signature St. Regis butler service.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Paseo Kanai 15, Solidaridad, 77730 Playa del Carmen, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 984 122 4800",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/cunxr-the-st-regis-kanai-resort-riviera-maya/overview/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/the-st-regis-kanai-resort-riviera-maya-playa-del-carmen.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Kosher meals can be ordered through the hotel from an outside certified kosher caterer (traveler reports). About 14 km from Chabad of Playa del Carmen; not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"Banyan Tree Mayakoba",description:"Ultra-exclusive private villa estate situated along tranquil emerald waterways and mangroves in Mayakoba. Every villa features a private heated plunge pool, lush walled gardens, and boat-accessible waterways.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Carretera Federal Chetumal-Puerto Juárez Km 298, 77710 Playa del Carmen, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 984 877 3699",website:"https://www.banyantree.com/mexico/mayakoba",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/g-banyan-tree-mayakoba-lagoon-villas.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"All-pool-villa resort. Banyan Tree has offered kosher meals through The Ember, its kosher menu (hotel PDF, 2022); confirm it still runs. About 8 km from Chabad of Playa del Carmen; not walkable for Shabbat."}],restaurants:[{name:"Bake & Roll by Mas Pan",description:"Kosher bakery and casual eatery serving fresh pastries, hearty lunch items, and popular for a festive Motzei Shabbat Melava Malka (Cash only in USD or MXN; NY-level pricing).",kosher:!0},{name:"Moshe Cube Kosher",description:"Middle Eastern kitchen serving kubbeh, shawarma, shakshuka, and grilled specialties (note: operates independently of the Chabad center; lower confidence on current rabbinic teudat hechsher certificate, please verify in advance before dining).",kosher:!0}],chabad:[{name:"Chabad of Playa del Carmen",address:"20 Avenida Nte. S/N, entre Calle 2 y Benito Juárez, Centro, 77710 Playa del Carmen, Q.R., Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Mendel Goldberg",phone:"+52 984 228 0425",website:"https://www.chabadplaya.org",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Bruncho Kosher (Chabad Playa del Carmen)",address:"20 Avenida Norte, between Calle 2 and Av. Juárez, Centro, Playa del Carmen",kashrus:"Chabad of Playa del Carmen (Glatt Meat)",phone:"+52 984 877 7210",website:"https://chabadplaya.org",type:"Israeli / Burgers / Grill",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-playa-kosher.webp"},{name:"Bake & Roll by Mas Pan",website:"https://chabadplaya.org/en/food/752/",address:"Calle 6 Norte & Av. Solidaridad (Mza 5 Lte 1), Centro, Playa del Carmen",kashrus:"Kosher Certified (Pas Yisrael / Dairy & Parve)",phone:"+52 984 314 7443",type:"Bakery / Casual Lunch / Melava Malka"},{name:"Moshe Cube Kosher",website:"https://www.moshecubekosher.com.mx",address:"Calle 38 Nte entre av. 10 y av. 20 norte, Gonzalo Guerrero, 77720 Playa del Carmen, Q.R., Mexico",kashrus:"Independent Kosher Supervision (lower confidence, please verify current teudat hechsher)",phone:"+52 984 173 0773",type:"Middle Eastern / Kubbeh / Grill",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-moshe-cube-kosher.webp"}],kosherGroceries:[{name:"Hilula Bakery",address:"Calle 8 Norte & Av. 20, Centro, Playa del Carmen"},{name:"Kosher Market (Chabad Playa del Carmen)",address:"Av. 20 Norte between Av. Juárez and Calle 2, Centro, Playa del Carmen"}],transportation:"Taxis operate on fixed union tariffs within town and the Riviera Maya corridor. For travel to Cancun, the ADO Alterna bus terminal runs clean, modern, air-conditioned buses every 10–20 minutes for about MX$124 (ADO quotes vary by departure), taking ~1 hr 5 min to Cancun Central Bus Station. Cozumel passenger ferries depart hourly from the downtown maritime terminal.",travelTips:["Communal Shabbat Atmosphere at Chabad: Chabad of Playa del Carmen hosts legendary Friday night dinners drawing 100+ Jewish travelers from around the globe, with enthusiastic singing, dancing, and abundant multi-course meals. Shabbat day lunch is equally welcoming and hearty.","Public Beach Access by Federal Law: In Playa del Carmen and across Mexico, all ocean beaches are legally public property. Even when beachfront resorts or beach clubs occupy the shoreline, public pedestrian access to and along the sand cannot be restricted or blocked.","Hilula Bakery for Shabbat Provisions: Located on Avenida 20 between Calle 6 and Calle 8, Hilula Bakery is the go-to spot for purchasing fresh Shabbat challah, babka, and baked goods prior to candle lighting.","ADO Alterna Express Bus to Cancun: Skip expensive long-distance taxis and head to the Playa del Carmen Alterna terminal (Av. 20 and Calle 12). Departures to Cancun run every 10 to 20 minutes for about MX$124 (ADO quotes vary by departure). The buses are clean, prompt, and arrive at Cancun Central Bus Station in about 1 hour and 5 minutes.","Excursion Planning on Avenida 5: When booking day excursions (Tulum ruins, cenotes, or the Punta Laguna monkey reserve) from Quinta Avenida kiosks, note that tours can sell out or close early during peak travel seasons and winter breaks. Book well in advance.","Playa del Carmen Taxi Rules & Union Rates: Uber is approved in Quintana Roo, but taxis are still the most common option. The local taxi union sets fixed zone rates. Always agree on the exact total fare with the driver before getting in, especially for trips outside the downtown grid.","Cozumel Ferry Logistics: Passenger ferries to Cozumel depart directly from the downtown maritime terminal by Parque Los Fundadores every hour on the hour. Because two distinct ferry companies (Ultramar and Winjet) alternate hourly departures, buy one-way tickets to keep your return schedule completely flexible.","Cenote Environmental Preservation: All visitors are required to take a cleansing shower before entering natural cenote pools. Chemical sunscreens, bug sprays, and body lotions are strictly prohibited to preserve the sensitive underground Mayan aquifer."],nearby:["Tulum","Cozumel","Akumal","Puerto Morelos"]},{id:"tulum",name:"Tulum",state:"Quintana Roo",country:"Mexico",region:"Caribbean",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/8aaad048e0bd55d7.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"4h 15m",Miami:"2h 00m",Jerusalem:"15h 45m",Paris:"10h 40m",London:"9h 55m"},weather:"☀️ 82°F",experiences:["Beaches","National Parks","Volcanoes"],mustDo:"Exploring the Tulum Mayan Ruins overlooking the ocean and biking along the Beach Road",description:"A trendy, boho-chic seaside escape famous for preserved Mayan cliffside ruins, luxurious eco-resorts, yoga retreats, and a warm Jewish community offering Shabbat options.",bestTimeToVisit:"November to December",nearestAirport:"Felipe Carrillo Puerto International Airport (TQO) / Cancún Airport (CUN)",airportDistance:"20 miles from TQO",attractions:[{name:"Tulum Archaeological Site",description:"Ancient Mayan walled city dramatically perched on high limestone cliffs above the sea.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/ac4bdb8c49e8aed4.webp"},{name:"Gran Cenote",description:"Famous half-cavern cenote populated by friendly freshwater turtles and small bats."},{name:"Sian Ka’an Biosphere Reserve",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/a36cb59b843f3b13.webp",description:"Massive UNESCO World Heritage site featuring wild dolphins, manatees, and wetlands."}],activities:[{name:"Biking the Beach Road",description:"Rent a beach cruiser to explore chic shops, jungle pathways, and pristine coves."},{name:"Floating down Sian Ka’an Canals",description:"Float gently down crystal-clear freshwater canals constructed by ancient Mayans."}],hotels:[{name:"Dreams Tulum Resort & Spa",description:"Secluded Spanish hacienda-style beachfront resort nestled on an expansive powdery white sand bay north of the Tulum ruins, featuring traditional Mexican arches, palm groves, and quiet oceanfront pools.",price:"$$$",address:"Puerto Juarez, Carretera Chetumal Km. 236, 77760 Tulum, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 984 871 3333",website:"https://www.hyattinclusivecollection.com/en/resorts-hotels/dreams/mexico/tulum-resort-spa/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/dreams-tulum-resort-spa.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 9 km north of Chabad of Tulum; taxi needed, not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"Hotel Bardo Tulum",description:"Adults-only mystical jungle sanctuary located in tranquil La Veleta, featuring secluded loft-style villas with private stone plunge pools, lush gardens, outdoor showers, and an ambient firepit lounge.",price:"$$$$",address:"Rio Otate & Rio Basca, 77760 Tulum, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 984 146 5431",website:"https://www.hotelbardo.mx/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/hotel-bardo-tulum.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 1.5 km (roughly an 18-minute walk) from Chabad of Tulum on Av. Kukulkan in La Veleta."},{name:"Be Tulum (BE DESTINATION Tulum)",description:"Chic barefoot-luxury jungle resort constructed with native stone, reclaimed wood, and limestone on Tulum’s south beach road, featuring rooftop plunge pools and oceanfront daybeds.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Carretera Tulum-Boca Paila Km 10, Zona Hotelera, 77780 Tulum, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 984 980 0678",website:"https://www.betulum.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/be-tulum-hotel-tulum.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 7.5 km from Chabad of Tulum via the beach road; taxi needed, not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"La Valise Tulum",description:"Exclusive 11-room boutique beachfront sanctuary famous for handcrafted artisan suites with open-air master beds that roll out onto private oceanfront terraces overlooking the Caribbean.",price:"$$$$",address:"Carr. Tulum-Boca Paila Km 8.7, Tulum Beach, Zona Hotelera, 77760 Tulum, Q.R., Mexico",phone:"+52 55 3439 1161",website:"https://lavalisetulum.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/la-valise-tulum-tulum.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 7 km from Chabad of Tulum; not walkable for Shabbat."}],restaurants:[{name:"Chabad Tulum Kosher Kitchen",description:"Glatt kosher home-style catering, fresh pita, falafel, and communal Shabbat dinners (note: operating hours and daily menu availability fluctuate seasonally with tourist traffic; lower confidence on fixed off-season daily hours, please verify in advance).",kosher:!0}],transportation:"Bicycles are the primary, most scenic way to traverse the Beach Road. Car rentals are helpful for long distance.",nearby:["Coba Ruins","Akumal","Muyil Ruins"],chabad:[{name:"Chabad of Tulum",address:"Villa Flor De Mayo, Av. Kukulkan Manzana 57 Lote 3, La Veleta, 77760 Tulum, Q.R., Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Netanel Binyamini",phone:"+52 984 347 0770",website:"https://chabadtulum.org",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Chabad Tulum Kosher Kitchen",photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp",address:"Villa Flor De Mayo, Av. Kukulkan Mz 57 Lt 3, La Veleta, Tulum",kashrus:"Chabad of Tulum (Glatt Kosher)",phone:"+52 984 347 0770",website:"https://chabadtulum.org",type:"Israeli Grill / Shabbat Catering / Mexican Kosher"}]},{id:"cabo-san-lucas",name:"Cabo San Lucas",state:"Baja California Sur",country:"Mexico",region:"Caribbean",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/ff99b06e4d625519.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"5h 45m",Miami:"4h 30m",Jerusalem:"17h 15m",Paris:"12h 00m",London:"11h 15m"},weather:"☀️ 82°F",experiences:["Beaches","Whale Watching","Off-Road Adventures"],mustDo:"Taking a boat tour to El Arco (The Arch) and whale watching in the Sea of Cortez",description:"A spectacular desert-meets-ocean destination at the southern tip of the Baja Peninsula, offering dramatic rock formations, luxury golf resorts, and an active Chabad catering to Jewish tourists.",bestTimeToVisit:"May to June",nearestAirport:"Los Cabos International Airport (SJD)",airportDistance:"28 miles",attractions:[{name:"El Arco & Land’s End (The Arch of Cabo San Lucas)",description:"Iconic granite archway standing 200 feet tall where the Sea of Cortez meets the Pacific Ocean, best experienced via glass-bottom boat tour."},{name:"Playa del Amor (Lover’s Beach) & Pelican Rock",description:"Secluded beach nestled between towering granite cliffs, accessible only by water taxi or boat, popular for snorkeling and swimming."},{name:"Playa El Médano (Medano Beach)",description:"Cabo's main safe-swimming beach, known for gentle waves, water sports like paddleboarding, and beachfront views toward El Arco.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d-playa-el-m-dano-medano-beach.webp"},{name:"Chileno Bay & Santa Maria Beach",description:"Chileno Bay and Santa Maria Beach are two Blue Flag beaches on the Tourist Corridor near Cabo San Lucas. Both bays are sheltered from strong waves, with calm, clear water popular for swimming and snorkeling. Chileno Bay has showers and restrooms."},{name:"Marina Cabo San Lucas Boardwalk",description:"Yacht harbor and marina in Cabo San Lucas with a pedestrian boardwalk lined with shops, restaurants, and sunset tour boats."},{name:"Mount Solmar & Cerro del Vigía",description:"Dramatic granite peak above Land’s End offering an exhilarating desert ridge hike with 360-degree ocean panoramas."},{name:"Mercado Orgánico San José & Mercado Popular",description:"Organic market in San José del Cabo (at Club La Huerta) with local crafts, produce, food stalls, and handmade goods, held on Saturdays."},{name:"Cabo Pulmo National Marine Park",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/51f8499c40fe70ee.webp",description:"Day trip · about 95 km from Cabo San Lucas. National marine park on the east coast of the Baja California Peninsula. It protects the northernmost coral reef in the eastern Pacific, estimated at about 20,000 years old. Known for snorkeling and diving."}],activities:[{name:"Glass-Bottom Boat Tour to El Arco & Land’s End",description:"Glide across crystal turquoise waters viewing marine life directly through glass hulls past sea lion colonies and dramatic granite spires."},{name:"Seasonal Humpback & Gray Whale Watching",description:"Encounter wild migrating whales breaching and singing in the Sea of Cortez and Pacific Ocean (Dec 15 – Apr 15)."},{name:"Wild Canyon Desert Adventures (ATVs & Ziplines)",description:"Race quads through rugged desert canyons and zip-line hundreds of feet above deep chasms on monster canyon lines."},{name:"Pelican Rock Water Sports & Scuba Diving",description:"Pelican Rock is a snorkeling and dive site off Cabo San Lucas in calm, clear Sea of Cortez water, a short boat ride from the marina. It starts as a small reef suitable for beginners, with rock formations, tropical fish and sea lions."},{name:"Deep-Sea Sportfishing Charters",description:"Depart from the marina to legendary offshore ocean banks targeting striped marlin, dorado, yellowfin tuna, and wahoo."},{name:"Luxury Desert Oceanfront Spa Experiences",description:"Spa experiences in the Cabo San Lucas area offering botanical treatments and oceanfront or garden settings."}],travelTips:["Pacific Ocean vs. Sea of Cortez Swimmability: Most open Pacific-facing beaches in Cabo have treacherous shorebreaks and severe undertows where swimming is strictly prohibited. Stick to designated swimmable beaches like Playa El Médano, Chileno Bay, and Santa Maria Beach.","Whale Watching Timing: Peak humpback and gray whale migration occurs between mid-December and mid-April. Early morning boat departures (8:00 AM–9:30 AM) offer the calmest sea surface and easiest whale spotting.","Kosher Meal Pre-Coordination Rule: Resort kosher dining is strictly NOT available on-demand at check-in. Coordinate with Rabbi Benny at Chabad of Cabo San Lucas at least 1–2 weeks prior to arrival to schedule catering and a mashgiach.","Corridor Transportation: The Tourist Corridor between Cabo San Lucas and San José del Cabo spans 20 miles. Rental cars or pre-arranged private transfers are far more cost-effective than relying on individual hotel taxi dispatches, which have steep flat union rates.","Shabbat Logistics in Los Cabos: Chabad is located in the Pedregal district of Cabo San Lucas. If staying out along the corridor (e.g. Solaz or Zadún), arrange Shabbat delivery boxes in advance as walking to shul from the corridor is not feasible."],hotels:[{name:"Waldorf Astoria Los Cabos Pedregal",description:"Spectacular 5-star ultra-luxury resort carved into towering granite cliffs at Land’s End, entered through a private torch-lit chandelier tunnel piercing the mountain. Every room features a private plunge pool, panoramic Pacific ocean views, and personal concierge service. The premier choice for Shabbat travelers due to its walking proximity to Chabad.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Cam. del Mar 1, Pedregal, 23455 Cabo San Lucas, B.C.S., Mexico",phone:"+52 624 163 4300",website:"https://www.waldorfastorialoscabospedregal.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/waldorf-astoria-los-cabos-pedregal-cabo-san-lucas.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.75 km (roughly a 10-minute walk by map routing) from the Cabo Jewish Center / Chabad of Cabo at Camino de la Plaza 135, Pedregal."},{name:"Zadún, a Ritz-Carlton Reserve",description:"Ultra-luxurious coastal sanctuary set where dramatic desert bluffs meet the Sea of Cortez, offering breathtaking desert-meets-ocean scenery. Standalone ocean-view pavilions each feature a private plunge pool and dedicated Tosoani private butler. Seasonal whale watching is frequently visible directly from private room terraces.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Blvd. Mar de Cortez, 23403 San José del Cabo, B.C.S., Mexico",phone:"+52 624 172 9000",website:"https://www.ritzcarlton.com/en/hotels/sjdzr-zadun-a-ritz-carlton-reserve/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/zadun-a-ritz-carlton-reserve-cabo-san-lucas.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Beyond Kosher Experience: separate meat and dairy kitchens supervised by Chabad of Cabo (K-abo Kosher), glatt meat, cholov Yisroel dairy, Shabbat menu. Mashgiach fee $200/day paid to Chabad; book at least 72 hours ahead. About 34 km from Cabo San Lucas."},{name:"Solaz, a Luxury Collection Resort, Los Cabos",description:"Contemporary architectural resort along the Tourist Corridor featuring an on-site certified kosher culinary program, cascading infinity pools, private ocean terraces, and multi-bedroom residences and suites with full kitchens and kitchenettes.",price:"$$$$",address:"KM 18.5 Carretera Transpeninsular CSL-SJC, Tourist Corridor, 23405 San José del Cabo, B.C.S., Mexico",phone:"+52 624 144 2100",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/sjdlc-solaz-a-luxury-collection-resort-los-cabos/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/solaz-los-cabos.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"On-site kosher program: breakfast at Cascabel, dairy lunch at Riccio di Mare, meat dinner at Mako, plus Shabbat meals. For Shabbat, room motion sensors (lights, A/C) and the electronic door lock can be turned off on request."}],restaurants:[{name:"Cabo Jewish Center kosher catering / Shabbat takeout",description:"Fresh, gourmet Glatt Kosher Mexican dishes, steaks, fish, and Shabbat takeout cooked fresh under Rabbi Hershcovich.",kosher:!0}],transportation:"Taxis are reliable but expensive. Car rentals are highly recommended to explore nearby San Jose del Cabo.",nearby:["San Jose del Cabo","Todos Santos","Cabo Pulmo"],chabad:[{name:"Cabo Jewish Center / Chabad of Cabo",address:"Cam. de La Pl. 135, Pedregal, 23450 Cabo San Lucas, B.C.S., Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Benzion (Benny) Hershcovich",phone:"+52 624 255 8901",website:"http://www.jewishcabo.org",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/cabo-jewish-center-chabad-of-cabo-cabo-san-lucas.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Ray's Cabo Kosher (at Cabo Jewish Center)",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/cabo-kosher-chabad-center.webp",address:"Cam. de La Pl. 135, Pedregal, Cabo San Lucas",kashrus:"Chabad of Cabo (Glatt Kosher)",phone:"+52 624 125 7932",website:"https://www.jewishcabo.org/kosher",type:"Mexican Kosher / Steaks / Shabbat Catering"}]},{id:"mexico-city",name:"Mexico City",state:"Distrito Federal",country:"Mexico",region:"Caribbean",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/5d885838c169261e.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"5h 15m",Miami:"3h 15m",Jerusalem:"16h 30m",Paris:"11h 30m",London:"10h 45m"},weather:"⛅ 72°F",experiences:["Wildlife","National Parks","Scenic Drives"],mustDo:"Wandering the historic neighborhoods of Polanco and Condesa",description:"A colossal historical metropolis and global culinary powerhouse. For Jewish travelers, Mexico City features a massive, incredibly prosperous community centered in the Polanco neighborhood, with dozens of top-tier kosher restaurants and markets.",bestTimeToVisit:"March to May",nearestAirport:"Benito Juárez International Airport (MEX)",airportDistance:"6 miles",attractions:[{name:"Chapultepec Castle (Castillo de Chapultepec)",description:"Historic hilltop castle overlooking Chapultepec Forest, one of only two royal palaces in North America once inhabited by monarchs (Emperor Maximilian I & Empress Carlota), now home to the National Museum of History."},{name:"Historic Spanish Inquisition Palace (Plaza Santo Domingo)",description:"Former headquarters of the Inquisition in colonial Mexico, built 1732–1736 with a tezontle facade and a corner entrance facing Plaza de Santo Domingo. It once held hearing rooms, trial rooms, secret chambers and a prison, and now houses a museum of medicine."},{name:"Museo Nacional de Antropología",description:"Premier world-class museum in Chapultepec showcasing profound pre-Columbian civilizations, featuring the monumental Aztec Sun Stone calendar."},{name:"Palacio de Bellas Artes",description:"Dramatic marble performance hall and museum in central Mexico City, featuring murals by Diego Rivera among other artists."},{name:"Museo Nacional de Arte (MUNAL)",description:"Architectural jewel on Calle de Tacuba housing five centuries of Mexican artistic heritage from the viceregal colonial era through 20th-century masters inside a regal neoclassical palace."},{name:"Palacio de Minería",description:"Neoclassical building in Mexico City's Centro Histórico, designed and built between 1797 and 1813 by Valencian sculptor and architect Manuel Tolsá to house the Royal School of Mines. Now part of UNAM's Faculty of Engineering, it houses the Tolsá Museum and temporary exhibitions."},{name:"Casa de los Azulejos (The House of Tiles)",description:"Exquisite 18th-century baroque count's residence whose exterior facade is covered on three sides in hand-painted blue-and-white Talavera ceramic tiles from Puebla."},{name:"Plaza de la Constitución (El Zócalo)",description:"Monumental central square and ceremonial bedrock of Mexico City, bordered by the National Palace and the buried foundations of ancient Tenochtitlan."},{name:"Xochimilco Canals (Embarcadero Nativitas)",description:"UNESCO World Heritage canal network in Xochimilco, navigated by colorful trajinera boats departing from Embarcadero Nuevo Nativitas, one of the main boat launches offering tours past floating gardens and chinampas."},{name:"Mercado de Artesanías La Ciudadela",description:"Long-running artisan market on Balderas in Mexico City's Centro, with about 350 vendors selling folk art and handicrafts from around Mexico, including alebrijes, Otomi textiles, jewelry and traditional clothing. Free entry."},{name:"Frida Kahlo Museum (The Blue House)",description:"Cobalt-blue house museum in Coyoacán, birthplace and lifelong home of Frida Kahlo. Preserves her personal belongings, artwork by Kahlo and Diego Rivera, folk art, and pre-Hispanic artifacts."}],activities:[{name:"Trajinera Boat Ride in Xochimilco",description:"Float along ancient Aztec agricultural canals on brightly decorated, flat-bottom boats."},{name:"Walking Tour of Polanco",description:"Stroll through tree-lined streets home to spectacular architecture and several synagogues."}],hotels:[{name:"JW Marriott Hotel Mexico City Polanco",description:"Sophisticated luxury hotel situated on Andrés Bello in the heart of Polanco overlooking Chapultepec Park, located di