,price:"$$$",address:"Liverpool 155, Juárez, Cuauhtémoc, 06600 Ciudad de México, CDMX, Mexico",phone:"+52 55 5228 9928",website:"https://www.nh-hotels.com/en/hotel/nh-collection-mexico-city-reforma",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/hotel-nh-collection-mexico-city-reforma-mexico-city.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"In Zona Rosa, about 4 km from Chabad Lubavitch in Polanco and 3 km from Gaucho Grill (kosher); taxi on weekdays, not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"Four Seasons Hotel Mexico City",description:"Grand hacienda-style colonial luxury sanctuary arranged around a serene, fountain-centered ivy courtyard on Paseo de la Reforma, at the edge of the Polanco district with world-class concierge service and tranquil garden atmosphere.",price:"$$$$$",address:"Av. Paseo de la Reforma 500, Juárez, Cuauhtémoc, 06600 Ciudad de México, CDMX, Mexico",phone:"+52 55 5230 1818",website:"https://www.fourseasons.com/mexico/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/four-seasons-hotel-mexico-city-mexico-city.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"On Paseo de la Reforma, about 2 km from Gaucho Grill (kosher, Polanco) and 3 km from Chabad Lubavitch at Calderón de la Barca 339."},{name:"Holiday Inn Express Mexico Basilica",description:"Modern, clean transit hotel located northeast of downtown, strategically situated for a fast, stress-free 15-20 minute morning drive to MEX Airport Terminal 2 ahead of heavy city traffic.",price:"$$",address:"Calzada de Guadalupe 54, Col. Ex Hipódromo de Peralvillo, Cuauhtémoc, 06250 Ciudad de México",phone:"+52 55 5704 7900",website:"https://www.ihg.com/holidayinnexpress/hotels/us/en/mexico/mexgu/hoteldetail",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/holiday-inn-express-mexico-basilica.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 7 km from Mexico City airport (MEX), per the hotel."}],restaurants:[{name:"Auguri Kosher Trattoria",description:"Top-rated kosher dining experience in Mexico City! Exceptional Italian trattoria serving pasta, risotto, and fish, featuring two dedicated sub-menus: Kosher Bamboo (Asian stir-fries & sushi) and Burger House (gourmet burgers & sandwiches).",kosher:!0},{name:"Gaucho Grill Polanco Kosher",description:"Renowned Glatt Kosher Argentinian steakhouse offering prime cuts, charcoal grill delicacies, empanadas, and warm soft-shell corn tortillas served in warming cloth pouches under KMD supervision.",kosher:!0},{name:"Pecorino Kosher",description:"Bustling, high-energy Chalav Yisrael Italian trattoria in Polanco serving artisanal wood-fired pizzas, handcrafted pastas, and fresh salads under KMD oversight.",kosher:!0},{name:"Sinai Deli & Bakery",description:"Classic Polanco kosher deli and bakery serving hearty breakfast platters, omelets, fresh pastries, and European baked goods under KMD.",kosher:!0},{name:"Ajla Gourmet Polanco",description:"Chic gourmet kosher breakfast spot and artisanal bakery in Polanco known for superb coffees, morning plates, and fresh baked breads.",kosher:!0},{name:"Wendy's Kosher Bakery",description:"Premier KMD-certified kosher bakery in Polanco featuring fresh Shabbat challot, babkas, pastries, and artisanal breads.",kosher:!0}],transportation:"DiDi has a very large presence in Mexico City and is often cheaper than Uber. Rush hours are roughly 6–10 AM, 1–3 PM (school traffic) and 6–9 PM. Always use licensed ride-hailing apps rather than hailing street cabs.",travelTips:["Rideshare App Comparison (DiDi vs Uber): Download DiDi before arriving in Mexico City. DiDi has extensive driver availability and is routinely 30–40% cheaper than Uber. If a DiDi driver’s final fare increases after the trip, tap the help button in the app to request an immediate refund back to the initial quote.","High-Altitude Dry Climate & Lip Care: Mexico City sits at an elevation of 7,350 feet (2,240m). The mountain air is notably dry and combined with urban smog can cause dry, chapped, or swollen lips. Keep ChapStick/lip balm on hand and drink plenty of bottled water (tap water is not potable).","Safety & Visible Police Presence: Mexico City maintains a heavy, reassuring tourist police presence across Polanco, Reforma, Centro Histórico, Roma, and Condesa. Daytime and early evening walking along main avenues is comfortable and safe.","MEX Airport Terminal 2 Departures: Arrive at least 2 hours before domestic flights.","Chapultepec Castle & Park Logistics: Chapultepec Castle is North America’s only royal-inhabited castle (Emperor Maximilian I and Empress Carlota). Note that public restrooms within the surrounding Bosque de Chapultepec park charge a small cash entry fee (~MX$5 coins required). The uphill walk takes 10–15 minutes.","Xochimilco Canal Booking at Embarcadero Nativitas: Head to Embarcadero Nuevo Nativitas (the largest dock). Trajinera boat rentals have an official rate set by the Xochimilco borough of MX$750 per hour for the whole boat (2025), not per person. Confirm duration and price before boarding.","KMD Kosher Certification: The main kosher certifier in Mexico City is KMD (Kashrut Maguen David), Horacio 1008, Polanco. Check kosher.com.mx for current certified products and establishments."],nearby:["Coyoacán","Puebla","Lomas de Chapultepec"],chabad:[{name:"Chabad CDMX - Polanco",address:"C. Calderón de la Barca 339, Polanco, Polanco III Secc, Miguel Hidalgo, 11550 Ciudad de México, CDMX, Mexico",rabbi:"Rabbi Mendel Mayzlesh",phone:"+52 55 5545 6770",website:"http://chabadofmexico.com",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Auguri Kosher Trattoria",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d3-auguri-kosher-trattoria.webp",address:"Av. Cordillera de los Andes 375, Lomas de Chapultepec (Lomas Virreyes), Miguel Hidalgo, CDMX",kashrus:"KMD Kosher Mexico (Chalav Yisrael / Kosher Dairy & Fish)",phone:"+52 55 5540 0500",type:"Italian / Kosher Bamboo Asian / Burger House"},{name:"Gaucho Grill Polanco",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venu